# Copy to .env.local and fill in real values once you wire up live channels.
# This is a *frontend* app — never put real secrets in VITE_-prefixed
# variables, since anything with that prefix is bundled into client JS and
# shipped to the browser. Real tokens belong in a backend/serverless
# function that the frontend calls; see README "From simulated to live data".

# Example of what a backend ingestion service would need (server-side only,
# NOT prefixed with VITE_):
# META_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# META_AD_ACCOUNT_ID=
# GOOGLE_ADS_DEVELOPER_TOKEN=
# GOOGLE_ADS_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_ADS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_ADS_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# GOOGLE_ADS_CUSTOMER_ID=
# GA4_PROPERTY_ID=
# GA4_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Public, non-secret config the frontend can read directly:
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
